s c3 is a standard support move. It is safe but slightly less dynamic than e5.\n3.  **N: g8-f6**: A flexible developing move that controls the center but doesn\'t occupy it with a pawn yet. It\'s good, but seizing space immediately is better against passive play.\n\nReason: Against a passive opening like 1. c3, the best strategy is to immediately occupy the center. Playing e5 is the most ambitious way to do this, as it restricts White\'s options and allows for rapid development of the kingside pieces. It punishes White\'s lack of ambition by taking the initiative.\n\nAnswer: P: e7-e5'}
