ed), maximizing central control is the best strategy.\n\nReason: The move P: d7-d5 allows Black to claim the center immediately, exploiting White's slow opening (c3). It establishes a space advantage and prepares for active piece development, placing Black in a statistically superior position.\n\nAnswer: P: d7-d5"}
