ck's position and gains a tempo, it does not have the immediate game-winning tactical force of the Queen check.\n3.  **N: g8-f6**: A standard developing move that controls the center. It is safe but ignores the immediate tactical opportunity to win the game.\n\nReason: The move **Q: d8-h4** exploits the exposed White King and the tactical geometry involving the f4 pawn. It forces a sequence where White must either lose their Queen (by blocking with Q-f2) or suffer decisive material loss (Rook at h1) and a mating attack after a failed block with g3. Maximizing the chance of winning requires seizing this tactical blunder immediately.\n\nAnswer: Q: d8-h4"}
